<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assakenoi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · Also known as Assacenians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Assakenoi were a people of the Swat and Buner valleys in what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> fought in 327 BCE. Their capital, Massaga, fell after a hard siege in which their queen Cleophis surrendered, and fugitives held out on the rock of Aornos. Many scholars link their name with the Ashvakas of Indian sources and with the Kambojas.</p></div>
